/* Ruler. */
"ruler.title" = "Ruler";
"ruler.measure" = "Measure the Screen";
"ruler.help" = "Hover and Plonk measures how far the pointer can travel each way before it meets an edge: the width of a row, the height of a bar, the gap between two things. Two numbers, drawn on the two lines they belong to, because the run across and the run down are separate answers. Drag instead for a straight-line distance. Click copies, Space takes a fresh picture of the screen, Escape finishes. Needs Screen Recording access, the same as a screenshot.";
"ruler.shortcut" = "Shortcut";
"ruler.detection" = "Detection";
"ruler.sensitivity" = "Edge sensitivity";
"ruler.sensitivityHelp" = "Lower stops at fainter borders and finds smaller things; higher walks through more before it calls anything an edge.";
"ruler.detectionHelp" = "How different one pixel has to be from the pixel beside it, on a scale of 255, before Plonk calls that boundary an edge. Ten suits most interfaces: gradients and shadows step by less, borders by more. Raise it for a photograph or a noisy video, where every pixel differs a little from the last.";

